<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahuitzotl</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1486">1486</a>–<a href="/years/1502">1502</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahuitzotl was the eighth tlatoani of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>, reigning from 1486 to 1502. He led extensive military campaigns that expanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> to its greatest extent, reaching as far as the Pacific coast and areas near present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>. He also oversaw the rededication of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/templo-mayor">Templo Mayor</a> in 1487.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahuitzotl.jpg" alt="Ahuitzotl" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ahuitzotl.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Ahuitzotl</b> (r. 1486–1502), the eighth Huey Tlatoani, was the greatest Aztec conqueror.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Under <b>Ahuitzotl</b> (r. 1486–1502) the Aztecs renewed the pressure through allied peoples of the Balsas region, but King Zuangua held the frontier, and the Aztecs never conquered the kingdom.</blockquote><a href="/empire/purepecha-empire">Purépecha Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Aztec Empire under <b>Ahuitzotl</b> sought to seize the isthmus, but Cocijoeza held out at the mountain fortress of Guiengola in a long siege in the late 1490s.</blockquote><a href="/state/zapotec-kingdom-of-tehuantepec">Zapotec Kingdom of Tehuantepec</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=19.44,-99.13&amp;year=1494" aria-label="Tenochtitlan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="1872 1444 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ahuitzotl"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2322 1714h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2322 1714h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=19.44,-99.13&amp;year=1494">What was here in 1494? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
